{"count": 1, "errors": [{"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-old", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-old", "field": "status", "reason": "'accepted' is not a valid status (draft, stable, deprecated) \u2014 run `khub upgrade` to migrate a legacy status"}, {"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-old", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-old", "field": "draft", "reason": "'draft' is retired; status carries the publish state \u2014 run `khub upgrade` to migrate it"}, {"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-old", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-old", "field": "sources", "reason": "sources holds bare entries ('knowledge/prd.md') \u2014 run `khub upgrade` to move them to references"}, {"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-old", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-old", "field": "body", "reason": "missing or out-of-order section '## Context' (template adr.yaml requires its headings in order)"}], "gaps": [], "body": {"words": 0, "sections": []}, "lenses": [{"code": "alternatives", "name": "A real alternative, not a strawman", "section": null, "instruction": "A decision with one option on the table is a description, not a decision. Name\nwhat else was genuinely considered and what it would have cost. If there was only\never one option, say that and say why \u2014 that is a constraint, and it belongs in\nContext."}, {"code": "consequences", "name": "The cost, not only the benefit", "section": null, "instruction": "Consequences that are all upside means the tradeoff has not been found yet. What\ngot harder? What can no longer be done cheaply? A reader six months from now is\nhere because something is painful and they want to know whether this record\npredicted it."}, {"code": "reversal", "name": "What would reverse this", "section": null, "instruction": "Name the observation that would make this the wrong call. Without it, nobody\nknows when to open a superseding record \u2014 and `supersedes` is the edge that makes\nthe history readable."}, {"code": "rule", "name": "A rule needs a requirement", "section": null, "instruction": "If this decision creates something the system must always or never do, that is a\n`requirement`, not a paragraph here. Add it and link it \u2014 `affects` carries the\nblast radius, and a rule buried in an ADR body is a rule nothing can check."}]}
